{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adventure-simulator-group/fabelgeist/pulls/992","id":5028704937,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPo01Gc8AAAABK7vyqQ","html_url":"https://github.com/adventure-simulator-group/fabelgeist/pull/992","diff_url":"https://github.com/adventure-simulator-group/fabelgeist/pull/992.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/adventure-simulator-group/fabelgeist/pull/992.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adventure-simulator-group/fabelgeist/issues/992","number":992,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Carry checked interpolation fractions through shared APIs","user":{"login":"segovb","id":70238035,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjM4MDM1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70238035?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/segovb","html_url":"https://github.com/segovb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/segovb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/segovb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/segovb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/segovb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/segovb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/segovb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/segovb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/segovb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/segovb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Walk/run blending passed a raw float through shared speed and cycle\ninterpolation, then admitted the same factor again for flight height. Both\ninterpolation methods now accept the existing `UnitInterval` type. Locomotion\nadmits its run factor once and reuses it across those operations; the\nlow-endurance speed producer also supplies an admitted blend.\n\nThe endurance smoothstep result is clamped to its intended `[0, 1]` range before\nadmission. `SpeedError` derives its error implementation and carries\n`FractionError`; animation uses its existing fraction-error conversion. Related:\n#780 and #726.\n\n## Validation\n\n[Hosted checks](https://github.com/adventure-simulator-group/fabelgeist/actions/runs/40452560923)\npassed at `df5f37a` on Linux and Windows. Raw logs confirm positive execution\nand zero failures in all 49 required rig groups and the three additional groups,\nincluding all four existing movement-speed tests and 98 shared animation tests.\n\nFourteen existing terrain cases remain ignored for explicit fixture, export or\nbenchmark requirements. Existing GPU, constraint and Windows portability checks\npassed. No tests, cases, helpers, assertions or doctests were added. Relevant\nsemantic baseline entries are unchanged.\n\n## Implementation context\n\nThe shared core `UnitInterval` remains the sole fraction owner. Scalar values\nare extracted inside the interpolation kernels and at the complementary bounce\ncalculation. This completes both speed callers and the cycle caller without a\nraw-float overload. The catalog build script compiles the same fraction owner\nand error derive as the runtime crate.\n","created_at":"2026-10-27T04:45:30Z","updated_at":"2026-10-27T06:09:58Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"16e1f4583e1a42944cc76af8e835b7218a578dfc","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adventure-simulator-group/fabelgeist/pulls/992/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adventure-simulator-group/fabelgeist/pulls/992/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adventure-simulator-group/fabelgeist/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adventure-simulator-group/fabelgeist/issues/992/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adventure-simulator-group/fabelgeist/statuses/df5f37abc8db96c3db69dd805f32ef1cf635dd59","head":{"label"